# Example project config. Normally you don't hand-write this — run:
#     sandbox new <project>
# which asks the questions and writes projects/<project>.conf for you.
#
# A project is one VM (claude-<project>) with its own GitHub identities.
# Tokens live in the macOS Keychain (sandbox secret set <name>); this file only
# references them by name. The FIRST identity is primary: it sets the default
# git commit identity, the active `gh` account, and owns the VM's SSH/signing key.
#
# This file is SHELL CODE — the launcher `source`s it. Keep it `chmod 600` and
# owned by you (that's what `sandbox new` does); it refuses to read a config that
# is group/world-writable. Quote any value containing spaces.

add_identity \
  --github-username my-user \
  --git-name        "My Name" \
  --git-email       me@example.com \
  --token-keychain  acme-my-user

# Agent opened by a bare `sandbox <project>`. Omit for the default (claude).
# See available agents with `sandbox agents`, or: sandbox <project> agent default <name>
use_agent claude

# Background daemons kept running in the VM with nobody attached — Claude Code's
# Remote Control, so the sandbox is drivable from claude.ai/code and the phone.
# Omit for "the agent above, if it declares one"; `use_daemon none` disables.
# use_daemon claude

# Optional: a second account whose token is used only for repos under one org.
# Routing is by longest "<host>/<org>" match; everything else uses the primary.
# add_identity \
#   --github-username my-bot \
#   --token-keychain  acme-my-bot \
#   --org-scope       github.com/some-org

# Arguments:
#   --github-username  GitHub login for this account            (required)
#   --token-keychain   Keychain item holding this account's PAT (required)
#   --git-name         commit author name    (primary identity only)
#   --git-email        commit author email   (primary identity only)
#   --org-scope        <host>/<org> to route to this token (repeatable)
#   --github-host      GitHub host (default: github.com)
#
# use_agent <name>     agent for a bare `sandbox <project>` (default: claude)
# use_daemon <name>    agent whose background daemon the VM keeps running
#                      (repeatable; default: the use_agent one; 'none' = off)
